    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A superbly located city home with excellent potential!\r\n\r\nNo. 22 Connolly Street offers the perfect balance of convenience and privacy—just a short stroll from Kilkenny city centre, yet tucked away in an established residential setting. This extended two-storey, end-of-terrace property (built c.1935) comprises a spacious four-bedroom home with a practical layout. Ideally suited to first-time buyers, investors, or those seeking a centrally located home. Positioned just off Butts Green, adjacent to Dean Street, the property benefits from an exceptionally convenient location within walking distance of all city amenities. Parliament Street is just 0.75km away, making commuting on foot an easy option.\r\n\r\nLoreto Girls' Secondary School, St. Canice’s Co-Ed Primary School and Ayrfield Medical Practice & pharmacy are located nearby. It’s locational virtues do not end here, however; St. Canice’s Church, St. Luke’s General Hospital, UPMC Aut Even Hospital, Kilcreene Orthopaedic Hospital, Dicksboro GAA Hurling Club, St. James’ Park playing field, Kilkenny CBS Primary School & Secondary School & a shop are also convenient. Beautiful walks along The River Nore Linear Park walk are also close by at Riverside Drive via Loreto View & Troy’s Lane. There is also a city bus stop located nearby on Dean Street which provides quick access to a variety of locations throughout and around the city centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\n•\tEntrance hall with stairs and understairs storage  1.7m x 2.9m\r\n•\tBedroom 1 (front-facing, wooden flooring) 2.61m x 2.4m\r\n•\tLiving room with side window, vinyl flooring. open fireplace with back boiler.  3.4m x 4.14m\r\n•\tKitchen/Dining area with fitted units, side window, vinly flooring, roof light & solid fuel stove with back boiler 4.05m x 2.65m\r\n•\tRear hall with access to yard\r\n•\tShower room (WC, WHB, electric shower) 1.8m x 2.02m  tiled flooring with enviroclad on walls. \r\n•\tBedroom 2 (rear-facing, wooden flooring) 2.2m x 3.92m\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n•\tLanding with side window\r\n•\tBedroom 3 (front-facing) 3.14m x 2.58m \r\n•\tBedroom 4 (rear-facing) 4.27m x 3.41m \r\n\r\nExterior\r\nThe property features a gated front driveway with a small patio and planting. A side entrance leads to a private rear yard, complete with a block-built shed for additional storage.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nThis home is ideally positioned close to a wide range of amenities including schools, medical centres, shops, and sports facilities. Scenic walks along the River Nore Linear Park and recreational facilities at St. James’ Park are all within easy reach. A nearby bus stop on Dean Street provides convenient public transport links throughout the city.\r\n\r\nAdditional Information\r\n•\tBER: G (Cert No. 119368702)\r\n•\tFloor Area: c. 92 sq. m.\r\n•\tServices: OFCH, mains water & sewerage, electricity\r\n•\tFixtures & fittings included\r\n•\tAlarmed throughout"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tPrime central location within walking distance of Kilkenny city centre\r\n•\tExtended end-of-terrace home\r\n•\t4 bedrooms\r\n•\tGated front driveway\r\n•\tSide pedestrian access to rear\r\n•\tRear yard with block-built shed\r\n•\tuPVC double-glazed windows\r\n•\tOil-fired central heating\r\n•\tAlarm system installed\r\n•\tClose to schools, Church, medical practice & pharmacy, playing fields, bus stop and local amenities\r\n•\tNature walks along The River Nore Linear Park, swimming in the River Nore & running in St. James’ Park are all a short distance away.\r\n•\tSt. Luke’s General Hospital, UPMC Aut Even Hospital & Kilcreene Orthopaedic Hospital are all a short drive away"
